{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_jjxhlkozsw7pnk3bh5v54chis53cwdxn5gatfeqqxa5lb4mougpq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete — the Rust translation matches the C byte-for-byte across all tested surface. **No divergences were found; no fixes to `src/lib.rs` were needed.**\n\n## Results\n\n| Gate | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo check` | clean, 0 errors/warnings |\n| `SYMBOLS.md` — symbol parity | 3/3 C symbols exported by Rust; 0 unresolved non-libc undefined |\n| `CONFIGS.md` — Phase B | 48/48 rows pass (~200k randomized cases, fixed seeds) |\n| `ERRORS.md` — Phase C | 30/30 rows + generic-boundary sweep pass (34 tests) |\n| Binary stdout compare | N/A — CMake builds only `libdriver.so`, Cargo only `[lib]` |\n| All feature combos | Cargo.toml has no `[features]`; verified for default / `--no-default-features` / `--all-features` × release + debug |\n\n## Artifacts in `translation/`\n- `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md` (30 rows + test-mapping), `CONFIGS.md` (48 rows)\n- `tests/common/mod.rs` — dual-`.so` libloading harness, `os_data`/`regmatch_t` ABI mirrors, seeded xoshiro256\\*\\* PRNG, guard-padded `uname` buffers, readable per-field sentinels\n- `tests/phase_b_valid.rs` (48 tests), `tests/phase_c_errors.rs` (34 tests)\n- `check_features.sh` — builds both libs, diffs `nm -D`, loops all feature combos × both profiles\n\n## Notable C quirks confirmed reproduced\n- `ARCHS` is **first-in-array wins**, not leftmost-in-string (`\"sparc x86_64\"` → `x86_64`)\n- Windows branch never sets `os_arch`/`os_codename`; `os_uname` is never written by any path\n- Unix branch searches for the arch only in the prefix *before* `\" [\"` (uname is NUL-terminated there first)\n- The `*(p + strlen(p) - 1) = '\\0'` idiom writes **one byte before the buffer** on empty strings — including 1-byte heap-metadata underflows (`\"Linux [\"`, `\"L [n: \"`, `\"L [n: 1.2 ()\"`). Reproduced identically via wrapping address arithmetic.\n- Non-participating capture group → `malloc(1)` + empty string, not `NULL`\n- No `NULL` check on `uname`/`os_header`/`pmatch` — crash parity asserted (same signal) in forked children\n- `regcomp` failure writes the exact diagnostic to stderr; compared verbatim in child processes\n\n## Harness validated by negative controls\nSix mutations injected into `src/lib.rs` were all caught before restoring: swapped `i386`/`i686` order (11 failures), dropped the build regex's optional group (27), `!result` inversion (73), skipped `trim_last_char` on `os_codename` (25), *adding* a `NULL` check the C lacks (3), and setting `os_arch` in the Windows branch (31).\n\nOne test-only bug was fixed during the run (`err29b`'s stdout filter didn't account for libtest's line prefix); nothing in `c_src/` was modified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3280,"cache_read_input_tokens":118497,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3280,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"08c47b1c-9021-445f-9179-52fb41c57c57","uuid":"88833d71-e821-4bd6-93f2-87f0bd1b9184","timestamp":"2026-09-05T09:49:10.833Z"}
